Aerie-Purpose: Turn Helium's services off and remove its hostnames, keeping only a user-configured https extension proxy.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: components/helium_services (helpers, BUILD.gn); settings services page placeholder and strings
Aerie-Kind: hook

Helium's services proxy (services.helium.imput.net) and its update host
(updates.helium.computer) are gone from the source. ShouldAccessServices() is
false, so component updates, bangs, spellcheck files, uBlock Origin assets and
browser updates have no origin and use the dummy one, which the network stack
refuses. The only origin left is the user's extension proxy, read from the
existing origin override pref and validated by components/aerie_services.
The plumbing stays, so Helium bumps conflict as little as possible.

